   old: `[[TIER-B: Cleon's close (S11): "You've been reading the strata. Old, older, oldest — I know, I read your face, you've dated these past anything the Compact admits." … "Here's what the strata can't tell you. These aren't the ruins of something. This is the *documentation* of something. Somebody wrote these down so the thing could be *built the same way twice*." … "In thirty years I never had the stone to match the text. You walked in with three floors." … "I don't think you're going to like what you've found, Karis. I've had a piece of it for a decade and I've never once slept well since." — the plan quotes this speech in four pieces with elisions; staged as Cleon's, to Karis, at his desk at the end of the 287th, with the bundle untouched on its shelf; coordinator to supply protected text]]`
   new: `"You've been reading the strata. Old, older, oldest — I know, I read your face, you've dated these past anything the Compact admits." He tapped the board. "Here's what the strata can't tell you. These aren't the ruins of something. This is the *documentation* of something. Somebody wrote these down so the thing could be *built the same way twice*." He sat back. "In thirty years I never had the stone to match the text. You walked in with three floors." A beat. "I don't think you're going to like what you've found, Karis. I've had a piece of it for a decade and I've never once slept well since."`

