editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-005/compiled-prompt.md:1791:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: the fifth day of thirty on the 284th**; on the stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall. It did nine miles on the 281st and twenty-two steps down on the 284th; the stick slipped once and he caught himself on the wall with the left hand. **He has sat three times.** He has confessed why he declined the second reading. He holds what Cael gave him and has not asked what read it. He does not know the mechanism, what Cael carries, the sum, or what is under the bar; he does no date arithmetic. He has said once that he has papers he will not show. He consented to be the fourth before he was asked and went through three counts as a hand, looking at his boots, "very ill" and then a little better. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He carries the kit case, still against the letter of Oryn's instruction; Oryn does not know.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-005/review-cold-prompt.md:2075:There was no healer on that side of a gate who would put hands on her for less than her name. The one who would have done it for a bowl of barley was five gates north, with a mule; and she would have asked first, and been told yes, and been grey for an hour afterward.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2075:There was no healer on that side of a gate who would put hands on her for less than her name. The one who would have done it for a bowl of barley was five gates north, with a mule; and she would have asked first, and been told yes, and been grey for an hour afterward.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2679:- **Cael:** nineteen. **There is no birthday in this book.** His own Arbiter woke at Kindling, its plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, and it went dark; he has no Path. He has **ten confirmed fragments**: Wind (Lira), Pressure (`the Bronze from Ardenmere` in spoken inventories), Iron (Brom), Compression (Reydan), Ember (Karis), Shadow (Seln; sealed; used exactly twice, at Ring and Stair), Storm (Daeva), Anchor (unnamed; used once each way), Blade (Ephram), and Tide (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; clinical; *ask first, every time*). Deployment since the Line: **twenty-seven**. **The still place** is not a fragment and is not counted: read three times, told to Oryn and then described to the other four, untouched since Oryn ordered him to write it down and stop touching it. His ribs have been quiet since the morning of day 129. The living purse holds 96 marks. Open accounts are listed below; `nothing owed` is false. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:2740:31. **KEEP — Millrace (298th evening–299th dawn).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The two healers look at each other and then at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more.") and takes the order without walking it back. Oryn's terms restated. "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient first ("May I?").** The readings: shoulder, arm ("Once is once more than I priced"), Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."), the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his."). **The deep reading**, with consent. **Rune turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** Withheld. Oryn's finding (§10). The leaf is offered: "Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table." Twelve and a mule at dawn.
