editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/movement-005/review-editorial-prompt.md:3611:**Vastin.** No office; no age stated. **Right knee: the fifth day of thirty on the 284th**; on the stick; no kneeling, no running, no wall. It did nine miles on the 281st and twenty-two steps down on the 284th; the stick slipped once and he caught himself on the wall with the left hand. **He has sat three times.** He has told Cael the rest of why he declined the second reading: the Ostrand reason stands as the cause, and beside it his private relief at never learning what a plate would say (glad of a right act for a wrong reason). He holds what Cael gave him and has not asked what read it. He does not know the mechanism, what Cael carries, the sum, or what is under the bar; he does no date arithmetic. He has said once that he has papers he will not show. He consented to be the fourth before he was asked and went through three counts as a hand, looking at his boots, "very ill" and then a little better; the clerk looked at him after the line was blotted, opened his mouth, and did not ask. He has not asked to join and nobody has spoken of it. He carries the kit case, still against the letter of Oryn's instruction; Oryn does not know.
