editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:23:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/state/pre-B6-reconciliation/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:45:The sensation-language of listening, kept to sensation; Thornwater in the back of autumn (ice on the trough, the grain going up the ladder past where they sleep); the tables' daily rhythm; the bowman's manner and words; the birthday's warmth and humor; the shape of each finding scene; all the windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-50.md:11:The row had changed again in the four days since the betting man's split line. Two of the food stalls by the pump had begun to bake in larger batches, and the pie woman had a boy helping her who had not been there before. Outside the Ironyard's side door, when Cael passed it, two men he knew by sight from the eel market were standing with Dace in the cold, talking with their hands, and Dace was listening with his pencil against his chest and the face he wore when he was being asked for something he had never given anybody. Cael heard *inside the doors*, and *three hours on their feet*, and *a copper a bowl*, and slowed without meaning to.
