editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:335:That was all. There were no extra lines tonight, or none that she wrote while he was standing there. He had been listening for them without meaning to, the way you listen for a second knock, and he noticed that he had been listening and did not like it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:989:"Wash, and carry, and boil, and fold, and watch." Alis fetched a small basin and a cloth and knelt down again. "Not anything else until the spring. Not anything with the Path. She says I don't know what I'm listening to yet, so I'm not to go poking about in anybody with it till I do." She dipped the cloth. "This'll sting."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:1905:*Again,* he thought, and Talis took a third step, and it came again: the hum in the dirt, and then, half a beat behind it, the foot. Every time. The ground knew where Talis was going to plant before Talis's foot got there. It said so, if you were listening with the right part of you, and Cael had not been. He had been listening with his eyes, at shoulders and hands, the way he listened to everybody. It had never once occurred to him that a tell could live in the ground.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:1971:"I'm listening to the floor."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-cold-prompt.md:2649:There was a narrow space between his cot and the wall, perhaps two strides long and one wide, where his bag stood and the cold came in under the window. He stood in it in his stockinged feet on the boards. The brothers were asleep. Yeni was asleep, or was lying with her eyes shut and listening, which with Yeni was the same thing.
