editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:103:The three primary repair measures named in the edition brief all pass their working ranges: sentence mean 13.23, long-sentence share 4.4%, and words per scene 1,016.8. Short-sentence share, paragraph median, and FK grade also pass the edition's accepted drift. The literal formula is not closely matched in distribution: median and mean are low, population spread is less than half the target, and readability is much easier. The pattern comes through on the page as brief dialogue/landing beats beside a limited band of 40–50-word narration, rather than the requested very broad continuum. If cadence is repaired, it should be a manual, sentence-by-sentence join of related short narration into clear medium-length sentences; the ≥40-word share is already at the top of its range, so extending the long tail would be the wrong lever.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:119:2. **Move the cadence modestly toward the literal formula without disturbing successful speech or action.** **Location:** exposition in Chapters 38–40 and Havel's explanatory paragraphs in Chapter 44; exclude protected text and both semifinals. **Observed issue:** mean 13.23 and median 9 are short of 14.6/11, SD 11.54 is far below ~26, and FRE 86.8 is much easier than 72.3, although all defined working ranges pass. **Effect on the reader:** related thoughts sometimes arrive as a sequence of similarly short units, while the documentary concepts themselves remain demanding; the sound can feel simpler than the idea. **Proposed scope:** a small same-author, sentence-by-sentence pass joining only clearly related short narration into readable 12–25-word structures; do not raise the ≥40-word share, already 4.4%, and do not alter dialogue, fight beats, or protected lines. **Strength to preserve:** the clean audio cadence, character-specific short speech, and sharp landing sentences.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-14.md:63:She had not been dancing to his drum, he understood. She had been listening to it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-14.md:81:The clock walked back to his mark and did not shake his hands out but stood very still. Cael could see that he was listening to his own drum, perhaps for the first time in his life, to make sure it was still there.
editions/monroe-1.3/tools/sol_recheck.sh:19:Read the FULL current movement, then follow $E/tools/RECHECK-TEMPLATE.md exactly: (1) brief items RESOLVED/PARTIAL/NOT with quoted evidence (diff -U0 vs pre-repair); (2) continuity; (3) formula — run \`python3 $E/tools/formula_metrics.py\` on the chapters, \`bash $E/tools/ed.sh overlap $B $N\`, \`bash $E/tools/ed.sh gates $B $N\`, \`bash $E/tools/sweep_probe.sh $B $N $N\`; (4) reader clarity; (5) listening proof on every chapter.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-48.md:259:He did not feel it go. That was the whole trouble with it, and he knew it, and it still caught him. One moment he was listening to a clerk explain a seal. The next, with no seam between them, the clerk was saying something else, and there was a short piece of the sitting he could not account for, as if somebody had turned a page in his head while he was not looking. He took the corner back at once. Nobody had looked his way. The inky-knuckled clerk, two chairs along, was writing.
