editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:5:**Coverage:** the seven chapters in declared order (34 Efficient · 35 The Second Look · 36 A Week Behind · 37 Nothing to Look Up · 38 A Door · 39 The Plan That Survives · 40 Tier Equivalent), plus chapter 33 for the seam, `packets/MOVEMENT-006.md` with all coordinator notes, `EDITION_BRIEF.md` (working ranges), BOOK_MAP, STATE_LEDGER through Movement 5, CANON_RULES, the Universe Bible, the seat's VOICE fight section, source Book 1 chapter 15, and the Book 2 / Book 4 source lines that name Sarel and Talis. Metrics are the coordinator's measured figures from `tools/formula_metrics.py`; I did not re-estimate. Source overlap: 0 unprotected runs, 0 protected (tool summary) — nothing to report.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-01-the-shattered/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:172:- **Proposed scope:** join clipped runs into one well-built sentence where they are one thought; give each chapter three to five deliberately long, readable sentences in walking, watching and letter passages where an action or a thought earns the length; drop "he said"/"she said" wherever the paragraph already shows the speaker. Aim at the working ranges, not the decimals. Expect a few hundred words to come out as a by-product. Leave the Log entries clipped; they are his voice.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-02-iron-circuit/manuscript/chapter-24.md:207:He was not watching for the breath any more. He had stopped listening for it somewhere in the walk back from the floor, without deciding to. He was not watching the purse, or the read, or the lead seam, or anything that had a page. There was only the next thing. Where Brom's lead shoulder was. Where his own left foot would go when it went. How much stone there was between them, and whether it was getting more or less.
