editions/monroe-1.3/book-03-no-path-given/state/movement-006/review-editorial.md:3:**Seat and standing.** This is a fresh-context editorial review, not self-review. The review seat is Claude Fable 5.1, standing in for the usual Sol seat (out of usage). The manuscript author was Claude Opus 5.5, a different model; I have no drafting history with this text and read it cold, in chapter order, before reading the author's report. It is a simulated cold read by a model, not a human read. Coverage: the seven supplied chapters (36,701 words by the supplied metrics), the preceding chapter 39 for the seam, the packet and its coordinator notes, the brief's working ranges and the 8-word reuse gate, the supplied canon evidence, the author's report (read as the author's map, not as evidence), and source chapters 15–17 for the reuse question. Measured metrics are the supplied ones; I did not re-estimate them. Everything else I measured myself is labelled with its method.
