# Targeted recheck — repair r1

I read the full current movement in chapter order and checked every changed region against `pre-repair/` with `diff -U0`. I then checked the movement against `BOOK_MAP.md`, the entry state and latest “After Movement” blocks in `STATE_LEDGER.md`, the Movement 5 join (especially chapters 35–36), `packets/MOVEMENT-006.md` including its coordinator notes, source chapter 17, and the later Keth-seam callback in Book 3 chapter 8.

This is an informed review-seat recheck (Sol via Codex), not author self-review, a fresh-context cold read, a human audience test, or independent demographic research.

